The workshop book is being indexed. (3× speed)

00:00:18.904 --> 00:00:19.193
Widen the slide-deck request. (3× speed)

00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:21.454
Write the source-grounded request. (3× speed)

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.563
Read the complete request.

00:00:23.563 --> 00:00:23.830
Send the question with the selected book. (3× speed)

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.322
Generate the answer from the selected source. (4× speed)

00:00:24.322 --> 00:00:26.035
Review the short English presenter deck. (3× speed)

00:00:26.035 --> 00:00:26.630
Generate the proposed outline from the selected book. (4× speed)

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:27.743
Open Studio and inspect the generated nine-slide outline. (3× speed)

00:00:27.743 --> 00:00:29.089
Review the outline before generating the deck. (3× speed)

00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:29.728
Generate the English slide deck from the approved outline. (4× speed)

00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:30.715
Open the generated English slide deck from the uploaded book. (3× speed)

00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:30.837
Present the generated deck and navigate through examples.

00:00:30.837 --> 00:00:33.664
Start the native slideshow

00:00:33.664 --> 00:00:33.877
Widen the native deck reader for full-slide readability.

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:35.408
Expand the native slide reader

00:00:35.408 --> 00:00:37.183
Advance with the actual native slideshow Right arrow key.

00:00:37.183 --> 00:00:41.010
A new definition changes the input context; it does not update the learned parameters.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.961
Compare structural parameter updates with input-level context changes.

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:49.863
Trace training from examples and prediction error to parameter updates.

00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:56.851
Trace ordinary inference through a fixed model to next-token probabilities.

00:00:56.851 --> 00:01:00.777
Inspect what the context window holds for this generation.

00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:05.753
Follow retrieved passages into the context, while the model stays fixed.

00:01:05.753 --> 00:01:12.178
Compare the inputs, actions and changes across training, inference and RAG.

00:01:12.178 --> 00:01:18.530
Explain independently why the connected manual database uses RAG rather than fine-tuning.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:18.906
Export the original generated deck for use without the author session.

00:01:18.906 --> 00:01:21.940
Inspect native deck export options

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.274
Download the original generated slide deck as PDF

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:23.685
Check the generation prompt and the original uploaded source.

00:01:23.685 --> 00:01:25.220
Inspect the deck prompt and source

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:28.083
The deck is grounded in the uploaded book; inspect its actual prompt and source.
